          "name": "tri",
          "version": "0.1.0"
        },
        "instructions": "Triangulator monitors Linux processes and their threads. For a past-day question, call list_incidents with the day's start and exclusive end in Unix seconds. It answers the question in one call. Use get_incident for stored evidence. State unknown incident coverage and all omissions. For current status, call status_now: it gives each target's verdict and findings, worst first, as the Triangulator dashboard shows them. Each target has a data object. State its gaps in the answer: a target that is not live, an unreadable view, limited access (no I/O or wait channels), a throttled sampler, packet loss, or an old last sample."
      }
    }
